title: Unintegrated content is a set difference with no memory.
pid: 5ffbadee-388e-4c7b-a281-e897afe37063
body: |2-
  What a subscribee as such shows of its content is its contains, less
  what the subscriber hides, less what the subscriber contains, compared
  after resolving IDs ('less_what_the_subscriber_integrates' in
  'server/refresh/goal.rs'). It is recomputed at each render; nothing
  remembers what was new last time.
  So the subscriber's own structure is its read receipt for the first
  layer: a child it contains or hides counts as dealt with. That is why
  a fresh fork shows nothing new. And it is why the trick does not
  reach further down: below the first layer the subscriber holds
  nothing to subtract.
